# Files NOT uploaded to Vercel.
#
# vercel.json blocks build/meta trees with a hand-maintained REDIRECT list
# (/docs/*, /tools/*, /.claude/*, ...). That list drifts: every new top-level
# directory is publicly served until someone remembers to add a rule — /tests/*
# was already exposed that way, and the native-app work added android/, ios/ and
# app/. This file is the deny-by-default complement: excluded paths are never
# uploaded, so they cannot be served at all.
#
# ⚠ DO NOT exclude api/ or lib/ — the serverless functions are api/*.js and they
# import from lib/ at runtime. Everything below is build-, docs- or app-only.

# Native app projects and the generated web bundle (can contain signing config)
android/
ios/
app/

# App toolchain. The serverless functions import ONLY Node built-ins (verified:
# no bare npm imports in api/ or lib/), so the site needs no npm install. Keeping
# package.json out of the upload also preserves Vercel's existing build detection
# for the website, which had no root package.json before the app work.
node_modules/
package.json
package-lock.json
capacitor.config.json

# Build scripts, tests, and internal docs — never served
tools/
tests/
docs/
.claude/
.github/

# Internal markdown docs anywhere in the tree (CLAUDE.md, HANDOFF.md, the root
# and per-folder READMEs, sources/PENDING_VERIFICATION.md, etc.). None is served
# as site content — the site is HTML — and CLAUDE.md/HANDOFF.md in particular
# carry internal handoff and security notes. vercel.json already REDIRECTS
# /CLAUDE.md and /HANDOFF.md to "/", but that only stops serving, not uploading:
# the files still shipped in every deployment, inflating Deployment Storage and
# leaning on a single redirect rule this file's header calls drift-prone. Excluding
# them here is the deny-by-default fix — never uploaded, so never served and never
# stored. robots.txt is .txt, not .md, so it is unaffected and keeps serving.
*.md

# Local secrets (belt and braces; also git-ignored)
revenuecat.json
*.keystore
*.jks
*.p8
*.p12
*.mobileprovision

# Un-deployed preview of the reworked homepage (docs/INSTAGRAM_GROWTH_STRATEGY.md
# follow-up). Owner asked to see it, explicitly NOT to put it live. It carries no
# content-review stamp, its streak figures are static placeholders, and the
# replace-vs-A/B decision is unmade. Kept in the repo so it is version-controlled
# and pullable; excluded here so Vercel never serves it. Delete this line when it
# has been gated and the owner decides to ship it.
homepage-v2.html

# For Parents page — RETIRED from the live site 2026-10-01 (owner decision), KEPT in the
# repo for reintroduction. It presented popular survey statistics as research and was never
# content-gated. To bring it back: delete this line and the /parents.html redirect in
# vercel.json, re-add the 'For Parents' item to the nav CANON in tools/sync-nav.mjs (and
# the dashboard tile), and run it through the content pipeline first. See HANDOFF.md.
parents.html

# Parked slavery content — TAKEN OFF the live site 2026-10-06 (owner decision: slavery is
# to be treated as a pastoral question, not an apologetics topic), KEPT in the repo for
# possible reintroduction. The three files were MOVED here from library/, answers/ and the
# root so the filesystem-scanning generators (essay-index, search-index, sources-index,
# our-sources, trust-numbers) drop them automatically. This dir is excluded so Vercel never
# serves them. To bring it back: git mv them to their original paths (_parked/abolition.html
# -> library/abolition.html, _parked/ev-m-abolition.html -> ev-m-abolition.html,
# _parked/did-christianity-end-slavery.html -> answers/did-christianity-end-slavery.html),
# remove the three /…/abolition + did-christianity-end-slavery redirects in vercel.json,
# re-wire the ev-s8 abolition card + evidence-library ARG_TAB/crawl-list + library/answers
# indexes + the pocket card + briefs entry + the compassion/equality cross-links, then
# re-run every generator. Also reconsider the slavery->pastor decline in api/ask.js.
_parked/
